### Why inventory-per-environment (not one file with groups)

Ansible's `--limit` and `-i` flags select the environment. Each environment is a complete, self-contained inventory. This means:

- Accidents are impossible. You can't `--limit prod` from a dev inventory file.
- Group_vars are scoped. `inventory/dev/group_vars/all.yml` only applies to dev hosts.
- Vault passwords are per-environment. A leaked dev password doesn't unlock prod.
- The `gradus` helper picks the inventory by name: `gradus bootstrap dev` reads `inventory/dev/hosts.yml`.

