## onboarding.yml

```yaml
#!/usr/bin/env ansible-playbook
---
# onboarding.yml — Bring a raw node into the fleet.
#
# Defines the Ansible interface: admin user exists, SSH works key-only,
# firewall is up, Python is ready. After this playbook, every node
# looks the same regardless of origin (VPS, VM, container, metal).
#
# Idempotent. Distro-agnostic. Converges to policy or fails loudly.
#
# First run (as root/OOB user):
# ansible-playbook -i inventory/dev onboarding.yml -u root -K
#
# Subsequent runs (as admin):
# ansible-playbook -i inventory/dev onboarding.yml -K
#
# After this: the node speaks Ansible. Apply layers (caddy-server.yml)..

- name: Define the Ansible interface
 hosts: all
 become: true
 gather_facts: false
 strategy: free

 vars:
 bootstrap_become: true

 pre_tasks:
 # --- Ensure Python exists (bootstrap prerequisite) ---
 - name: Ensure Python and sudo
 ansible.builtin.raw: |
 test -x /usr/bin/python3 || {
 apt-get update -qq
 DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive apt-get install -y -qq python3 sudo
 }
 changed_when: false
 when: ansible_facts.distribution is not defined

 - name: Gather facts
 ansible.builtin.setup:

 - name: Assert required inputs
 ansible.builtin.assert:
 that:
 - admin_pubkey is defined
 - deploy_pubkey is defined
 - admin_password_hash is defined
 fail_msg: >-
 Missing admin_pubkey, deploy_pubkey, or admin_password_hash.
 Ensure group_vars and vault are configured for this inventory.

 # =====================================================================
 # ROLES: distro-agnostic convergence
 # =====================================================================
 roles:
 # Python, sudo, gnupg, python3-apt. Makes the node Ansible-ready.
 - role: robertdebock.bootstrap

 # EPEL repository. No-op on Debian, essential on RHEL/Fedora.
 - role: robertdebock.epel

 # Full package upgrade. Patches stale images.
 - role: robertdebock.update

 # Unattended-upgrades. Keeps the box patched automatically.
 - role: robertdebock.auto_update

 # Ensure cron is installed and running.
 - role: robertdebock.cron

 # Time sync. Installs chrony (Debian) or ntpd (RHEL).
 - role: robertdebock.ntp

 # SSH hardening. NOTE: verify role internals before enabling.
 # See tasks/sshd_crypto.yml for what we supplement.
 # - role: robertdebock.openssh

 # Intrusion prevention. Replaces sshguard.
 - role: robertdebock.fail2ban

 # Firewall. ufw (nftables backend) on Debian, firewalld on RHEL.
 - role: robertdebock.firewall

 # Umask in ~/.bashrc. Supplement only — login.defs is the real fix.
 - role: robertdebock.umask

 # Permanent users: admin + deploy. Idempotent.
 - role: robertdebock.users

 # =====================================================================
 # CUSTOM TASKS: what the roles can't do
 # =====================================================================
 tasks:
 # --- Umask: must precede user creation (chicken-and-egg) ---
 # The robertdebock.umask role only edits ~/.bashrc for EXISTING users.
 # login.defs must be written BEFORE robertdebock.users creates admin/deploy.
 # However, since users role is idempotent, on first run the home dirs
 # may already exist with wrong perms. We fix them after.
 - name: Umask in login.defs
 ansible.builtin.include_tasks: tasks/login_defs_umask.yml

 - name: Umask in profile.d (system-wide, all shells)
 ansible.builtin.include_tasks: tasks/profile_d_umask.yml

 - name: Ensure home dir modes are correct (fix chicken-and-egg)
 ansible.builtin.file:
 path: "/home/{{ item.name }}"
 mode: "0750"
 state: directory
 loop: "{{ users }}"

 # --- SSH crypto hardening (supplements openssh role) ---
 - name: sshd crypto drop-in
 ansible.builtin.include_tasks: tasks/sshd_crypto.yml

 # --- Deploy access (rrsync forced command) ---
 - name: Deploy key and sites root
 ansible.builtin.include_tasks: tasks/deploy_access.yml

 # --- Audit: verify the interface holds ---
 - name: Install audit script
 ansible.builtin.copy:
 src: files/audit-listeners.sh
 dest: /usr/local/sbin/audit-listeners.sh
 owner: root
 group: root
 mode: "0755"

 - name: Run audit
 ansible.builtin.script: files/audit-listeners.sh
 changed_when: false

 # --- Handoff ---
 - name: Interface defined
 ansible.builtin.debug:
 msg:
 - "Node normalized. Interface contract holds."
 - "Expected listeners: {{ firewall_services | map(attribute='name') | join(', ') }}"
 - "Apply a layer: ansible-playbook -i {{ inventory_dir }} caddy-server.yml -K"

 handlers:
 - name: Reload sshd
 ansible.builtin.systemd:
 name: ssh
 state: reloaded
 listen: "reload ssh"

 - name: Reload nftables
 ansible.builtin.systemd:
 name: nftables
 state: reloaded
 listen: "reload firewall"

 - name: Restart fail2ban
 ansible.builtin.systemd:
 name: fail2ban
 state: restarted
 listen: "restart ids"
```

## tasks/login_defs_umask.yml

CAN THIS BE REPLACED BY USING A BETTER ORDER OF OPERATIONS AND THIS ROLE: https://github.com/robertdebock/ansible-role-umask

```yaml
---
# Writes UMASK 027 to /etc/login.defs.
# Must run BEFORE robertdebock.users creates admin/deploy,
# so their home directories get mode 0750 from useradd.
#
# On re-runs where users already exist, this is still correct:
# login.defs affects future useradd calls, and the file
# chmod task in bootstrap.yml fixes existing homes.

- name: Set UMASK in login.defs
 ansible.builtin.lineinfile:
 path: /etc/login.defs
 regexp: '^UMASK\s'
 line: 'UMASK {{ umask_value }}'
 backup: true
```

## tasks/profile_d_umask.yml

```yaml
---
# System-wide runtime umask for all login shells.
# Covers bash, sh, zsh — anything that sources /etc/profile.

- name: Write /etc/profile.d/umask.sh
 ansible.builtin.copy:
 dest: /etc/profile.d/umask.sh
 content: |
 # UC-Gradus: enforce {{ umask_value }} for all login shells
 umask {{ umask_value }}
 owner: root
 group: root
 mode: "0644"
```

## tasks/sshd_crypto.yml

CAN THIS BE DONE USING THE ROLE https://github.com/robertdebock/ansible-role-openssh

```yaml
---
# Supplements the openssh role (or replaces it if the role
# doesn't expose the knobs we need).
#
# sshd reads all files in sshd_config.d/ alphabetically and
# keeps the FIRST value it encounters per option. The robertdebock
# openssh role writes to sshd_config directly (to be verified),
# so our drop-in in sshd_config.d/ sorts before it in the include
# chain and wins.

- name: Write crypto hardening drop-in
 ansible.builtin.template:
 src: templates/50-crypto.conf.j2
 dest: /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/50-crypto.conf
 owner: root
 group: root
 mode: "0644"
 validate: 'sshd -t -f %s'
 notify: reload ssh
```

## templates/50-crypto.conf.j2

```
# UC-Gradus: SSH crypto policy
# This file sorts after the openssh role's config (if any)
# and before any future overrides.

# Only modern algorithms
KexAlgorithms curve25519-sha256,curve25519-sha256@libssh.org,diffie-hellman-group16-sha512,diffie-hellman-group18-sha512
Ciphers chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com,aes256-gcm@openssh.com,aes128-gcm@openssh.com
MACs hmac-sha2-512-etm@openssh.com,hmac-sha2-256-etm@openssh.com

# Session limits
MaxAuthTries 3
MaxSessions 10

# No forwarding
AllowAgentForwarding no
AllowTcpForwarding no
X11Forwarding no
GatewayPorts no

# Timeout
ClientAliveInterval 300
ClientAliveCountMax 2

# Environment
AcceptEnv LANG LC_*
